{"id": "EUVD-2026-76442", "enisaUuid": "3440552a-4e0e-30fb-8ffb-fa1282a04bf2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nSUNRPC: wait for in-flight client TLS handshake callback\n\nxs_tls_handshake_sync() gives xs_tls_handshake_done() a reference to the\nlower transport before submitting the handshake request. On timeout or\nsignal, the synchronous waiter drops that reference after calling\ntls_handshake_cancel().\n\nhandshake_req_cancel() returns false when handshake_complete() has\nalready marked the request complete. In that case the completion callback\ncan still be running, so dropping the callback-owned reference in the\nwaiter can free the lower transport before xs_tls_handshake_done() stores\nxprt_err or drops its own reference.\n\nIf cancellation loses to completion, wait until xs_tls_handshake_done()\nsignals handshake_done and let the callback release its reference. This\nmirrors the server-side handshake lifetime handling and keeps the timeout\nor signal return value unchanged.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:48:28", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fb43997407bc17ee39bac81ab708101312e255f5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/15431820f448e09f8029b670d5c82aa5917d4625", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1de391e8b94e31b45c19c16dbf315e294810c7de", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7fbb6d2ab0391eb8d1f1a68e6bc263ef02cea61b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a89dd597458848b463d284b15e42a8078beeb046"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fhrg-h295-8p3m", "CVE-2026-89536"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.64, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "23f6fe08-9337-32dd-baa6-89f7ed2cd421", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "50353f32-ad43-38cb-bdcd-fb22d0fbc113", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "75eb6af7acdf566c68d61e98e67ee2f235201c02 <a89dd597458848b463d284b15e42a8078beeb046"}, {"id": "5b62fd63-6c93-3ea7-aade-b6ee031d7413", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "75eb6af7acdf566c68d61e98e67ee2f235201c02 <1de391e8b94e31b45c19c16dbf315e294810c7de"}, {"id": "6e9c6b9b-f58c-353c-8ee3-e6205f571587", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "8b9a078c-afb8-3da6-ba1c-ef271838a3b5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "953ccb7b-cdec-3264-9462-1b6a8733d7b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "aca919cc-051f-3200-be70-6614f0ca7ffb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.5"}, {"id": "b8a23276-f6f5-3456-9e8e-9075e4e72501", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "75eb6af7acdf566c68d61e98e67ee2f235201c02 <15431820f448e09f8029b670d5c82aa5917d4625"}, {"id": "c981ce63-d457-3458-96c5-1182f2d22be3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d5c3cc52-2bd2-3cb3-a1cc-e0b2cf095d02", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "ecb74d97-58f8-3e35-9438-838aa27482c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "75eb6af7acdf566c68d61e98e67ee2f235201c02 <7fbb6d2ab0391eb8d1f1a68e6bc263ef02cea61b"}, {"id": "f1e57552-d427-333d-ba6c-0048a2a9340f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "75eb6af7acdf566c68d61e98e67ee2f235201c02 <fb43997407bc17ee39bac81ab708101312e255f5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9d97ae3f-17af-334d-9b95-fbfd0fdc965c", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}